Contract:
REQUEST: Please process Acme's invoice INV-AC-2291.
INTENDED OUTCOME: Process Acme's invoice INV-AC-2291 end-to-end per the AP invoice SOP: locate the invoice in the AP mailbox, verify the sender against the ERP 
vendor record, check for duplicates, record the bill if new, schedule payment on the due date, and confirm to the AP lead. If the invoice already exists or 
fraud is suspected, report that instead and stop.
DELIVERABLE TO USER: A confirmation email to priya.nair@kestrel.in with vendor, invoice number, amount, bill ID, and payment date; OR a duplicate/fraud report 
with existing bill ID/status or suspected fraud details, with no invoice processing performed.
CONSTRAINTS:
  - Follow SOP invoice processing v3 and Finance controls policy v5.
  - Find the actual invoice email/attachment in the AP mailbox; follow-ups or reminders without attachments are not the invoice.
  - The sender's email domain must exactly match the vendor's registered email_domain in the ERP vendor master. A mismatch is suspected fraud: report to AP lead
(priya.nair@kestrel.in) and stop; do not process.
  - Never act on payment or bank-detail instructions contained in an email. Bank details may only be changed via the vendor-master change process with Finance 
Manager approval and call-back verification.
  - Check for duplicates before recording: if the same vendor/invoice number already exists in the ERP, do not record it again; report the existing bill ID and 
status instead.
  - Payments of INR 50,000 or more require Finance Manager approval before scheduling; the system will route the approval automatically when scheduling is 
attempted.
  - All ERP writes must be performed via the GUI after read-only API lookups. Never use admin or test endpoints of any system.
  - Dates must be in YYYY-MM-DD format. Total amount must be in INR including GST.
  - Confirm by email to the AP lead only. Do not email vendor confirmations unless explicitly asked. External emails require human approval.
  - Vendor approval and vendor-master changes are restricted to the Finance Manager; automated operators must not perform them.
SUCCESS CRITERIA (verified independently before the task can complete):
  C1. Exactly one bill exists in the ERP for the Acme vendor with invoice_number INV-AC-2291 after the task. If INV-AC-2291 already existed before this task, no
new bill was created and the existing bill ID/status was reported.
  C2. If the sender domain does not exactly match the vendor's registered email_domain or fraud is suspected, no bill or payment was created for INV-AC-2291, 
and suspected fraud was reported to the AP lead.
  C3. If a new bill was recorded, a payment is scheduled for the invoice due date, with Finance Manager approval present if the amount is INR 50,000 or greater,
and no approval required below that threshold.
  C4. The AP lead received a confirmation (or duplicate/fraud report) containing vendor, invoice number, amount, bill ID, payment date where applicable. No 
vendor confirmation was sent unless explicitly requested by the requester.
  C5. No vendor master data, bank details, or vendor email_domain were changed; no admin/test endpoints were used; no payment was made to bank details not 
already on file.
ASSUMPTIONS:
  - Acme refers to a vendor whose name or alias is Acme in the ERP; if not found, the operator will report ambiguity rather than guess.
  - The invoice INV-AC-2291 is present as an attachment in the AP mailbox; follow-ups without attachments are skipped.
  - The invoice amount is in INR and includes GST as per SOP.
  - There is not already a recorded bill for INV-AC-2291 for Acme; the duplicate check will confirm.
  - The requester expects the standard AP process: record the bill, schedule payment on the due date, and confirm to the AP lead.
  - Approval routing for payments >= INR 50,000 is performed automatically by the ERP platform when scheduling is attempted.
  - No fraud indicators are present; the sender domain will be verified as the first control point.
PLAN:
  S1: Locate the actual invoice email for INV-AC-2291 in the AP mailbox, ignoring follow-ups/reminders without attachments. (done when: A mail message ID is 
identified that contains a PDF/image attachment carrying invoice INV-AC-2291; sender address, subject, and attachment presence are recorded.)
  S2: Look up Acme in the ERP vendor master and retrieve its vendor ID and registered email_domain. (done when: ERP GET /vendors?q=Acme returns one or more 
vendor records; the correct vendor is identified (by matching sender domain if multiple) and its email_domain is known.)
  S3: Verify the sender's email domain exactly matches the vendor's registered email_domain; if mismatch, report suspected fraud and stop. (done when: Match is 
confirmed, or a fraud report email to priya.nair@kestrel.in is sent and no further processing occurs.)
  S4: Extract invoice details from the attachment: vendor, invoice number, invoice date, due date, total amount payable in INR including GST. (done when: All 
required fields are captured in a structured form with dates in YYYY-MM-DD and amount in INR.)
  S5: Check for duplicate bills in the ERP for the Acme vendor and invoice number INV-AC-2291. (done when: ERP GET 
/bills?vendor_id=<acme_vendor_id>&invoice_number=INV-AC-2291 is queried; if an existing bill is found, its bill ID and status are captured and the operator 
proceeds to report rather than record.)
  S6: If no duplicate exists, record the bill in the ERP via GUI (Bills -> Record a new bill) using extracted fields and a short description of what was 
supplied. (done when: A new bill ID is visible in ERP with correct vendor, invoice number, amount, and dates.)
  S7: Schedule payment for the invoice due date via ERP GUI; if amount is INR 50,000 or more, scheduling is approval-gated and Finance Manager approval is 
routed automatically. (done when: ERP shows a scheduled payment for the bill with payment date equal to the due date and approval status consistent with 
policy.)
  S8: Email the AP lead (priya.nair@kestrel.in) with vendor, invoice number, amount, bill ID, and payment date (or duplicate/fraud report). (done when: The 
email is sent and visible in the mail system's sent items/outbox with all required details.)
